+<body>
+  <main class="page-shell">
+    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
+      <p class="eyebrow">Cat care basics</p>
+      <h1 id="page-title">Frequently asked questions about cats</h1>
+      <p class="hero-copy">
+        Practical answers for new and curious cat people, from feeding routines
+        to playful behavior and everyday care.
+      </p>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="faq-card" aria-label="Cat FAQ">
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-knead" id="question-knead">
+          <span>Why do cats knead blankets or people?</span>
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="answer-knead" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-knead" hidden>
+          <p>
+            Kneading is a comforting behavior that starts when kittens nurse.
+            Adult cats often knead when they feel relaxed, safe, or especially
+            fond of the person or surface they are touching.
+          </p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-food" id="question-food">
+          <span>How often should I feed my cat?</span>
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="answer-food" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-food" hidden>
+          <p>
+            Most adult cats do well with two measured meals per day, though some
+            prefer smaller meals more often. Kittens, seniors, and cats with
+            medical needs may require a schedule recommended by a veterinarian.
+          </p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-water" id="question-water">
+          <span>Why does my cat like running water?</span>
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="answer-water" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-water" hidden>
+          <p>
+            Moving water can seem fresher and more interesting to cats. A clean
+            bowl placed away from food, or a pet fountain, can encourage better
+            drinking habits.
+          </p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-scratch" id="question-scratch">
+          <span>How can I stop unwanted scratching?</span>
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="answer-scratch" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-scratch" hidden>
+          <p>
+            Scratching is natural and helps cats stretch, mark territory, and
+            maintain their claws. Offer sturdy scratching posts near favorite
+            resting spots, reward use, and redirect gently from furniture.
+          </p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
